# Permanent solutions only

Always ship the lasting fix. Do not leave temporary workarounds, bandaids, or "we'll fix it later" shortcuts.

## Required

- Fix the root cause, not the symptom.
- Prefer the correct architecture, data model, or API even when a hack would be smaller.
- Remove dead paths and temporary guards once the real fix is in.
- If a prior shortcut exists (`TODO`, `FIXME`, `hack`, `ponytail:` ceiling), replace it with the permanent fix when you touch that area.

## Forbidden unless the user explicitly asks for a stopgap

- Hardcoded one-off special cases that only cover the reported path
- Swallowing errors / silent retries that hide the real failure
- Copy-paste duplicates instead of fixing the shared function
- Feature flags, kill switches, or comment-out blocks left as the "solution"
- "Good enough for now" patches that will break the next caller

## When a shortcut is unavoidable

Only if the user asks for a temporary workaround, or an external blocker makes the permanent fix impossible right now:

1. Say so clearly in the reply.
2. Name the permanent follow-up.
3. Do not present the shortcut as the finished solution.
